+# Specialty Directory Inverts the Held-By Direction in a Read Model
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The specialty directory lists every specialty the clinic knows, each with the veterinarians holding it. Two properties of the existing model stand in the way.
+
+The `Vet`-to-`Specialty` association is mapped in one direction only. `Specialty` carries no collection of the veterinarians holding it, so no existing type answers the question the page asks.
+
+A specialty no veterinarian holds must still appear. The veterinarian collection alone cannot produce it, because an unheld specialty is reachable from no veterinarian.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Bidirectional association** — add an inverse collection to `Specialty`, mapped by the existing join table, and read the holders off the entity.
+2. **Join-direction query** — declare a repository query projecting the join table into specialty-and-holder rows, and assemble the page from that result.
+3. **Read-model inversion** — load the specialties and the veterinarians separately and group them in a stateless domain service.
+
+## Decision
+
+Option 3. `SpecialtyRepository` supplies every specialty in name order, mirroring `PetTypeRepository`. `VetRepository.findAll` supplies the veterinarians; it is cached and its specialties are eager-fetched. A stateless domain service groups the two into the directory's read model, and `Specialty` gains no back-reference.
+
+Option 1 was rejected because an inverse collection widens an entity's surface for one read-only page, and eager-fetching both directions risks loading the whole vet-specialty graph from either side. Option 2 was rejected because it places the page's grouping rule in a query string, where it is reachable only through a JPA context.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The entity mapping and all three vendor schemas are untouched.
+- The grouping rule is unit-testable with real `Vet` and `Specialty` objects, without a web or persistence context.
+- No second cache is introduced. The directory reads through the existing vet cache and therefore inherits its un-evicted state, recorded as an open question in [system-design.md](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey).
+- Each request reads every specialty and every veterinarian. The page carries no paging by requirement, so the read is bounded only by the size of the clinic's roster.
+- Two specialties stored under one name produce two entries, since grouping is by stored identity rather than by name.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the types realizing this decision
+- [2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md](2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md) — why the types sit in the `vet` package
+- [2026-07-31-server-side-rendering-with-thymeleaf.md](2026-07-31-server-side-rendering-with-thymeleaf.md) — the rendering and message-bundle rules the page follows
