+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-specialtydirectory-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse of that directory: every specialty it knows, each shown by its stored name with the veterinarians who hold it `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]`. A holder is named in full, first name then last name. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, shown as held by none. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it — the page lists specialties, not the roster. Every specialty appears together on one page. The page is reachable at its own address, `/specialties.html`, and nothing links to it. No navigation entry and no link from another page belongs to this capability. Its wording obeys the language requirements that bind every page.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the specialties the clinic knows, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed by its stored name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a specialty one or more veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each holder is shown by first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the directory is opened, then it is listed as held by none.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is not shown anywhere on it.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given every specialty the clinic knows, when the directory is opened, then all of them are shown together, with no paging control.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the page's address, when it is requested directly, then the page is served, and no other page links to it.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A clinic that knows no specialty leaves the page empty rather than failing.
+2. Specialties are listed in a stable order, and so are the veterinarians under each.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
